Networking without network threads.

The request and stream schedulers advance their transfers in passes on the
engine RunLoop instead of on worker threads. A pass is queued when work is
added, when the host reports socket data (pumpNow), and on curl's own timeout.
Stream connects run on a per-stream multi handle so they never block. Client
callbacks are always posted, never made from inside curl. TLS trusts the CA
bundle staged in the engine file system; network state reports online.

